00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:30.100
It starts off with Dwight being so pleasant, trimming his fingernails at work.
开头是德怀特表现得非常“惬意”，在办公室里剪指甲。

456
00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:31.140
Why, Dwight?
为什么啊，德怀特？

457
00:21:31.280 --> 00:21:31.520
Why?
为什么？

458
00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:34.260
We reveal, guess who's sitting next to him?
我们揭晓一下，猜猜谁坐在他旁边？

459
00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:35.100
Not Jim.
不是吉姆。

460
00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:37.300
And no longer the temp, it's Ryan.
也不再是那个临时工了，是瑞安。

461
00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:40.440
And can we talk about that Ryan got a whole new look?
我们能聊聊瑞安换了全新的造型吗？

462
00:21:40.600 --> 00:21:42.260
A bunch of people look a little different.
很多人看起来都有点不一样了。

463
00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.120
A little better.
看起来好了一些。

464
00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:47.640
He like cut his hair short and it's not floppy anymore and it looks like there's some gel.
他把头发剪短了，不再是那种软塌塌的样子，看起来还抹了点发胶。

465
00:21:47.960 --> 00:21:50.180
Anyway, this is the new improved Ryan.
总之，这就是全新升级版的瑞安。

466
00:21:50.400 --> 00:21:52.640
He's no longer the temp and he's got a whole new look.
他不再是临时工了，而且换了全新的造型。

467
00:21:52.640 --> 00:22:01.080
Well, then we move to Pam typing at her desk and she looks longingly over at Jim's old desk at Ryan.
好吧，然后镜头转到帕姆在办公桌前打字，她深情地望向吉姆原来的座位，也就是瑞安现在坐的地方。

468
00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:05.000
And this is when we flash back to Casino Night.
这时候我们闪回到了“赌场之夜”。

469
00:22:05.500 --> 00:22:06.200
Oh my God.
天哪。

470
00:22:06.240 --> 00:22:08.880
And we get an extension of the scene.
我们看到了那个场景的后续。

471
00:22:09.280 --> 00:22:12.860
We see that a whole thing happen after the kiss.
我们看到接吻之后还发生了一连串的事。

472
00:22:13.120 --> 00:22:13.540
Yes.
没错。

473
00:22:13.740 --> 00:22:17.840
They both admit to each other that they've wanted to do that for a long time.
他们都向对方承认，他们想这么做已经很久了。

474
00:22:18.180 --> 00:22:20.980
And Pam is like, I think we're drunk.
帕姆说，我觉得我们喝醉了。

475
00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:22.960
And Jim's like, I'm not drunk.
吉姆说，我没喝醉。

476
00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:23.600
Are you drunk?
你喝醉了吗？

477
00:22:23.740 --> 00:22:26.040
And she's like, no, no, I'm not drunk.
她说，没有，没有，我没喝醉。

478
00:22:26.220 --> 00:22:28.600
And then Jim goes in for another kiss.
然后吉姆又凑过去吻了她。

479
00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:30.100
Yeah.
是的。

480
00:22:30.300 --> 00:22:31.600
And she's like, I can't.
她说，我不能这样。

481
00:22:31.720 --> 00:22:33.360
And he's like, you're going to marry him?
他说，你真的要嫁给他吗？

482
00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:34.720
And you were like, yes.
而你当时说，是的。

483
00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:39.040
I know we had a lot of fan questions about this.
我知道粉丝们对这一段有很多疑问。

484
00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:44.640
Jenna Adams, Matt Grasso, Brett Hedges, Alyssa Dunn, and many others wanted to know,
珍娜·亚当斯、马特·格拉索、布雷特·赫奇斯、艾丽莎·邓恩，还有许多其他人都想知道，

485
00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:49.600
did we film the continuation of the kiss scene at the same time as Casino Night?
我们是在拍摄“赌场之夜”时就拍好了接吻的后续吗？

486
00:22:49.600 --> 00:22:53.000
Or did we have to recreate the moment for Gay Witch Hunt?
还是为了《同性恋猎巫行动》那一集重新补拍的？

487
00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:56.300
Guys, we had to recreate it.
伙计们，我们必须重新补拍。

488
00:22:56.700 --> 00:22:57.980
We had to recreate it.
我们必须重新补拍。

489
00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:01.560
And this is like, thank God for Ken Kuapis.
谢天谢地有肯·夸皮斯在。

490
00:23:01.880 --> 00:23:03.260
Thank God we had the same director.
谢天谢地我们还是由同一位导演执导。

491
00:23:03.620 --> 00:23:06.820
So we had to redo everything.
所以我们必须把一切重做一遍。

492
00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:13.620
Kim Ferry had taken photos of every side of my head, and she painstakingly redid my hairdo.
金·费里拍下了我头部各个角度的照片，然后费尽心思地还原了我的发型。

493
00:23:13.840 --> 00:23:15.760
Thank God my dress still fit.
谢天谢地我的裙子还穿得进去。

494
00:23:15.760 --> 00:23:18.420
But we added a new camera angle.
但我们增加了一个新的摄像机角度。

495
00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:19.680
I don't know if you noticed that.
不知道你们有没有注意到。

496
00:23:19.840 --> 00:23:21.840
They set up the spy shot from the kitchen,
他们设置了从厨房拍过来的偷拍视角，

497
00:23:21.840 --> 00:23:31.660
and then they put an extra camera inside the conference room shooting through the blinds so that you could finally now see Pam's face and Pam's reaction.
然后又在会议室里放了一台额外的摄像机，透过百叶窗拍摄，这样你们终于能看到帕姆的脸和她的反应了。

498
00:23:31.660 --> 00:23:39.140
I don't know if this is true, Jenna, and I don't know if it's just because I had this information in my brain that I knew you had to recreate this moment.
我不知道这是不是真的，珍娜，我也不知道是不是因为我脑子里有这个信息，所以我知道你们必须重现这一刻。

499
00:23:39.800 --> 00:23:44.260
This is ridiculous, but I do feel like you're at a different position on Jim's desk.
这听起来很荒谬，但我确实觉得你在吉姆桌子上的位置变了。

500
00:23:44.280 --> 00:23:46.900
I feel like you're a little further down.
我觉得你稍微往后挪了一点。

501
00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:51.780
I feel like you're not right by the phone, which is where you were because you had hung up the phone.
我觉得你当时并没有在电话旁边，而你之前是在那儿的，因为你刚挂了电话。

502
00:23:52.500 --> 00:23:52.900
Right?
对吧？

503
00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:54.820
So this is just a little catch.
所以这只是个小破绽。

504
00:23:55.420 --> 00:23:57.140
No, Angela, your catch is good.
不，安吉拉，你发现得很好。

505
00:23:57.140 --> 00:24:06.100
I think in order to get that camera angle through the blinds in the conference room, we had to scoochie scooch just a few inches down the desk.
我想为了让摄像机能穿过会议室的百叶窗拍到那个角度，我们不得不把桌子往旁边挪了几英寸。

506
00:24:06.380 --> 00:24:06.700
Wow.
哇。

507
00:24:07.200 --> 00:24:07.700
Wow.
哇。

508
00:24:07.900 --> 00:24:09.600
I'm impressed that you caught that.
你能发现这一点我很佩服。

509
00:24:09.740 --> 00:24:10.900
I mean, we tried to...
我是说，我们试着……

510
00:24:10.900 --> 00:24:13.780
We tried our best to fool people.
我们尽力去糊弄大家了。

511
00:24:13.780 --> 00:24:18.260
But we had to re-kiss again because you'll notice that...
但我们不得不重新亲一次，因为你会注意到……

512
00:24:18.260 --> 00:24:24.740
And that was like, by the way, they brought out like a still frame image to me and John of us kissing.
顺便说一下，他们拿了一张我和约翰接吻的剧照给我们看。

513
00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:27.720
And they were like, okay, so now, Jenna, your arm is here.
他们说，好了，珍娜，你的手臂在这儿。

514
00:24:28.020 --> 00:24:29.000
Your hand is here.
你的手在这儿。

515
00:24:29.140 --> 00:24:31.580
John, this is how you had your hand around her.
约翰，你当时是这样搂着她的。

516
00:24:32.020 --> 00:24:39.500
So we had to like painstakingly recreate the pose and everything so that it would look seamless.
所以我们必须费尽心思去重现那个姿势，好让画面看起来天衣无缝。

517
00:24:39.500 --> 00:24:43.260
But if you watch, we kiss and we pull away and start talking immediately.
但如果你仔细看，我们亲完分开后马上就开始说话了。

518
00:24:43.660 --> 00:24:44.400
So that was...
所以那是……

519
00:24:44.860 --> 00:24:47.000
It was all recreation.
那全是后期重拍的。

520
00:24:47.800 --> 00:24:48.680
How awkward.
真尴尬。

521
00:24:48.900 --> 00:24:49.900
Just think about this.
想想看。

522
00:24:50.180 --> 00:24:50.980
Here's your job.
这就是你的工作。

523
00:24:51.100 --> 00:24:53.480
You go to work one day and someone's like, here's your job today.
你某天去上班，有人对你说，这是你今天的工作。

524
00:24:53.680 --> 00:24:57.980
You need to find a photo of Jenna and John kissing as Jim and Pam.
你需要找一张珍娜和约翰以吉姆和帕姆身份接吻的照片。

525
00:24:58.140 --> 00:24:59.140
You need to print it out.
你需要把它打印出来。

526
00:24:59.220 --> 00:25:00.760
I need multiple copies.
我要多印几份。

527
00:25:00.920 --> 00:25:03.600
A lot of people are going to be studying this photo.
很多人都会研究这张照片。

528
00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:06.220
Then we're going to take it to Jenna and John.
然后我们要把它拿给珍娜和约翰看。

529
00:25:06.400 --> 00:25:07.580
We're going to recreate the moment.
我们要重现那一刻。

530
00:25:07.820 --> 00:25:09.140
I want it high res.
我要高清的。

531
00:25:09.140 --> 00:25:10.560
I want it in color.
我要彩色的。

532
00:25:11.040 --> 00:25:12.500
Print me a bunch of photos of them kissing.
给我打印一堆他们接吻的照片。

533
00:25:12.740 --> 00:25:13.200
Okay, thanks.
好的，谢谢。

534
00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:15.200
Yeah, that was pretty much it, Ange.
没错，安吉，基本上就是这样。

535
00:25:15.300 --> 00:25:16.280
That was pretty much it.
基本上就是这样。

536
00:25:16.400 --> 00:25:17.220
That was someone's job.
那是某人的工作。

537
00:25:18.540 --> 00:25:19.580
That's so crazy.
太疯狂了。

538
00:25:19.920 --> 00:25:20.200
All right.
好吧。

539
00:25:20.280 --> 00:25:22.860
Well, I love that little behind the scenes moment, Jenna.
我喜欢那个幕后小花絮，珍娜。

540
00:25:23.100 --> 00:25:29.560
I love that you acknowledge that you weren't kissing by the phone where you hung up with your mom.
我喜欢你承认自己当时并没有在电话旁边，也就是你跟妈妈挂断电话的地方。

541
00:25:30.200 --> 00:25:31.100
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

542
00:25:31.360 --> 00:25:33.400
But I want to get into the episode a little bit here.
但我想稍微聊聊这一集的内容。

543
00:25:33.600 --> 00:25:35.780
Now, Toby is in Michael's office.
现在，托比在迈克尔的办公室里。

544
00:25:35.960 --> 00:25:37.540
We're at two minutes, 13 seconds.
时间在两分十三秒。

545
00:25:37.800 --> 00:25:38.880
He's talking to Toby.
他在和托比谈话。

546
00:25:39.140 --> 00:25:41.560
Because apparently Michael was inappropriate again.
因为显然迈克尔又表现得不妥当了。

547
00:25:41.760 --> 00:25:48.240
You know, he basically gives Oscar a hard time for liking Shakespeare in Love instead of Die Hard.
你知道，他基本上是因为奥斯卡喜欢《莎翁情史》而不是《虎胆龙威》而为难他。

548
00:25:48.380 --> 00:25:48.560
Yeah.
是啊。

549
00:25:48.560 --> 00:25:52.140
And maybe doesn't word it very well, you guys.
而且他表达得可能不太好，各位。

550
00:25:52.340 --> 00:25:53.740
Doesn't word it the beSt.
措辞不是最恰当的。

551
00:25:53.880 --> 00:26:04.400
But when you watch this scene, watch Steve's performance as Michael realizes that Oscar is actually gay.
但当你观看这一幕时，请留意史蒂夫的表演，看迈克尔是如何意识到奥斯卡其实是同性恋的。

552
00:26:04.960 --> 00:26:05.320
Yes.
没错。

553
00:26:05.320 --> 00:26:08.640
Like, his transformation of going from like, yeah, yeah, yeah, whatever.
就像他那种转变，从那种“是啊，是啊，是啊，随便吧”的状态。

554
00:26:08.780 --> 00:26:09.360
Yeah, no, I know.
是啊，不，我知道。

555
00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:14.160
And then it's such a great acting moment, in my opinion.
在我看来，那真是一个非常棒的表演时刻。

556
00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:16.880
Steve, once again, just blew me away.
史蒂夫再一次让我惊艳了。

557
00:26:16.880 --> 00:26:20.920
And here's my other thing I need to point out in this scene, you guys.
还有一点我必须在这一幕中指出来，伙计们。

558
00:26:21.080 --> 00:26:26.920
And I don't know, maybe it's controversial, but you know who I think outed Oscar?
我不知道，也许这很有争议，但你们知道我认为是谁让奥斯卡出柜的吗？

559
00:26:27.640 --> 00:26:28.160
Toby!
托比！

560
00:26:28.440 --> 00:26:28.720
Toby!
托比！

561
00:26:29.320 --> 00:26:29.660
Yes!
没错！

562
00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:38.500
This is going to come up later, Angela, because Jan is going to come into the office and reprimand Michael for outing Oscar to the rest of the office.
安吉拉，这事儿之后还会提到，因为简会来到办公室，训斥迈克尔向办公室其他人泄露了奥斯卡的性取向。

563
00:26:38.840 --> 00:26:48.720
And she goes on this whole speech where she's like, it is a big moment in a person's life, and they should be able to choose how and when they come out to people.
她发表了一大通演说，大意是说，这对一个人来说是人生中的重大时刻，他们应该有权选择如何以及何时向他人出柜。

564
00:26:48.720 --> 00:26:52.800
And the whole time, I just kept thinking, Toby!
而整个过程中，我一直在想：托比！

565
00:26:53.260 --> 00:26:54.900
Toby outed Oscar!
是托比让奥斯卡出柜的！

566
00:26:55.140 --> 00:26:57.380
Oscar told that to Toby in confidence.
奥斯卡是私下告诉托比的。

567
00:26:58.120 --> 00:26:58.740
Yes!
没错！

568
00:26:59.000 --> 00:27:04.000
And Toby told the one person who would not be able to contain that information.
而托比偏偏告诉了那个最藏不住话的人。

569
00:27:04.340 --> 00:27:07.980
Here's two people Toby could have told if he wanted everyone to know.
如果托比真想让大家都知道，他本可以告诉这两个人。

570
00:27:08.260 --> 00:27:09.680
Michael and Kelly.
迈克尔和凯莉。

571
00:27:10.220 --> 00:27:10.840
Correct.
没错。

572
00:27:10.840 --> 00:27:11.400
There you go.
就是这样。

573
00:27:11.800 --> 00:27:12.440
There you go.
就是这样。

574
00:27:12.900 --> 00:27:18.280
So now, I mean, Michael decides he's got to apologize to Oscar.
所以现在，我的意思是，迈克尔决定他必须向奥斯卡道歉。

575
00:27:18.800 --> 00:27:21.000
Of course, it's not in private.
当然，不是私下道歉。

576
00:27:21.280 --> 00:27:24.340
He just walks over to the accounting desk pod.
他直接走到了会计部的办公区。

577
00:27:24.580 --> 00:27:28.080
You have Kevin and Angela exchanging some glances.
你可以看到凯文和安吉拉交换了几个眼神。

578
00:27:29.920 --> 00:27:35.860
And then Michael's like, well, maybe, you know, we could go out to dinner and you could explain to me how it works.
然后迈克尔说，嗯，也许，你知道，我们可以出去吃顿饭，你可以向我解释一下这是怎么回事。

579
00:27:35.940 --> 00:27:37.760
And Oscar's like, yeah, that would be wonderful.
奥斯卡说，好的，那太棒了。

580
00:27:37.980 --> 00:27:39.580
Yeah, we should do that.
是啊，我们应该那样做。

581
00:27:40.000 --> 00:27:40.840
Oh, Angela.
噢，安吉拉。

582
00:27:41.160 --> 00:27:44.120
Angela, I have the script for Gay Witch Hunt.
安吉拉，我有《同性恋猎巫行动》的剧本。

583
00:27:44.500 --> 00:27:46.000
You know how I have some scripts?
你知道我有一些剧本吧？

584
00:27:46.300 --> 00:27:47.600
Oscar, did Oscar improvise?
奥斯卡，奥斯卡是即兴发挥的吗？

585
00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:48.400
That would be wonderful.
那太棒了。

586
00:27:48.840 --> 00:27:51.180
Steve and Oscar improvised that whole couplet.
史蒂夫和奥斯卡即兴发挥了那整段对话。

587
00:27:51.380 --> 00:27:52.840
That is not in the script.
剧本里没有那段。

588
00:27:53.160 --> 00:27:54.140
I wondered.
我就在想。

589
00:27:54.480 --> 00:27:54.600
Yeah.
是啊。

590
00:27:54.820 --> 00:27:55.500
When Steve...
当史蒂夫……

591
00:27:55.500 --> 00:27:56.040
Now, listen.
现在，听着。

592
00:27:56.180 --> 00:27:57.100
I say improvised.
我说即兴发挥。

593
00:27:57.240 --> 00:28:00.500
Sometimes the writers were on set and they would pitch lines to the actors.
有时编剧会在片场，他们会给演员提议台词。

594
00:28:00.760 --> 00:28:05.300
But I know that in this particular episode, Steve and Oscar took a lot of liberties.
但我知道在这一集中，史蒂夫和奥斯卡做了很多自由发挥。

595
00:28:05.300 --> 00:28:08.660
They are both masterful improvisers.
他们俩都是即兴表演的大师。

596
00:28:08.900 --> 00:28:09.240
Yes.
没错。

597
00:28:09.460 --> 00:28:13.100
And they improvised a lot on these scenes.
他们在这些场景中即兴发挥了很多。

598
00:28:13.240 --> 00:28:22.300
And I believe that Steve improvised that line about maybe we could go have a beer and you could just tell me how you do that to other dudes.
我相信史蒂夫即兴说出了那句关于“也许我们可以去喝杯啤酒，你可以告诉我你是怎么对其他男人做那种事的”。

599
00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:24.780
And that Oscar was like, yes, Michael.
而奥斯卡回答说，好的，迈克尔。

600
00:28:25.260 --> 00:28:26.600
That sounds wonderful.
那听起来太棒了。

601
00:28:27.320 --> 00:28:28.260
That's wonderful.
那真是太棒了。

602
00:28:28.460 --> 00:28:29.020
What a wonderful...
多么美妙的……

603
00:28:29.760 --> 00:28:31.380
I can't wait.
我迫不及待了。

604
00:28:31.540 --> 00:28:31.960
Yeah.
是啊。

605
